   "name": "Practical: Investigating Temperature Changes",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Practical: Investigating Temperature Changes"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Aim:"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- To perform a calorimetry study of the reaction between HCl and NaOH"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Apparatus:"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Dilute hydrochloric acid\n- Dilute sodium hydroxide solution\n- Styrofoam (polystyrene) calorimeter & lid\n- 25 cm<sup>3</sup> measuring cylinder\n- Thermometer & stirrer"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Simple calorimeter"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/02/Calorimeter-Styrofoam-Cup.png",
   "file": "assets/4e00cbce6215-calorimeter-styrofoam-cup.png",
   "alt": "Calorimetry equipment set up ",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***A lid is required to prevent heat loss***"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Method:"
  },
  {
   "type": "ordered",
   "md": "1. Using a measuring cylinder, place 25 cm<sup>3</sup> of the NaOH solution into the calorimeter\n2. Measure and record the temperature of the solution\n3. Add 5 cm<sup>3</sup> of the dilute HCl and stir\n4. Measure and record the highest temperature reached by the mixture\n5. Repeat steps 1 – 4 increasing the amount of acid added by 5 cm<sup>3</sup> each time"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Results:"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Record your results in a suitable table"
  },
  {
   "type": "table",
   "md": "| **Volume of acid (cm**<sup>**3**</sup>**)** | **Temperature (**<sup>**o**</sup>**C)** |\n|---|---|\n| 5 |   |\n| 10 |   |\n| 15 |   |\n| 20 |   |\n| 25 |   |"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Plot a graph of the results and draw a line of best fit, using the graph to determine what volume of acid causes the biggest change in temperature"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Conclusion:"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- The larger the difference in the temperature the more energy is absorbed or released"
  }
 ]
}